1
00:00:02,400 --> 00:00:10,320
Hi, I'm Charlie Chapman, a relatively new indie iOS developer, and I'd like to introduce you to my new podcast Launched.

2
00:00:10,880 --> 00:00:27,440
Leading up to the launch of my app, Dark Noise, to the App Store this past summer, I found myself devouring any podcasts I could find that were interviewing app developers or really any other type of creator talking about the process of building and releasing their creation out into the world.

3
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:31,360
So I decided to make a podcast dedicated to that exact thing.

4
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:37,280
The show will launch in mid January, and if you're listening now, you've already found the right place to subscribe.

5
00:00:37,520 --> 00:00:39,680
If you want to follow along my journey leading up to launch.

6
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:46,560
Give me a follow on Twitter at underscore chuck e c or the podcast handle is at launchedfm.

7
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:55,920
Plus, I've set up a subreddit at reddit.com slash r slash launchedfm that you can use to post your ideas or recommendations for who I should interview on the show.

8
00:00:56,640 --> 00:01:04,480
To be honest, this whole thing is kind of an experiment, so I hope you're all excited to join me on this journey to see what this project is going to eventually become.

9
00:01:05,280 --> 00:01:13,360
I love feedback and the first few months especially are probably going to have some growing pain, so please let me know what you think of each episode on Twitter or Reddit.

10
00:01:13,920 --> 00:01:24,080
I'll be playing around with different formats, different lengths, different levels of formality, so getting a sense of what you all think is going to be paramount to the success of this project as a whole.

11
00:01:24,640 --> 00:01:33,680
And before I go, if you're really hungry for interviews with app developers now, I'd highly recommend checking out the Indie Beginnings podcast by Will Bishop.

12
00:01:33,920 --> 00:01:35,360
I'll throw a link in the show notes.

13
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:40,080
He already has a few episodes out and they've been really great so far, so I would definitely check that out.

14
00:01:40,800 --> 00:01:45,920
Well, so I guess that's about it, so tell all your friends and I'll see you all in mid January.
